  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inclusive green growth in Egypt (Phase II)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IGGE Phase II was already part of the project trajectory envisioned per the original Project Document, proposed as a logical follow-on to Phase I, characterized by an increasing focus on institutionalization and scale-up. As a result of Phase I highly satisfactory performance (as per the external evaluation conducted), the project partners have highlighted the need and expressed their support for the development of Phase II. Building on the successes of Phase I, IGGE Phase II aims to contribute to transforming the market system to be more conducive to MSME growth and enable inclusive and sustainable economic and industrial development within the green and circular economy. In Phase II, activities will intensify the implementation and mainstreaming of already developed instruments while working toward closing remaining gaps, focusing on integrating finance, policy, technology, production and market domains, expanding its beneficiaries pool (empowering mid-market enterprises alongside MSMEs and expanding geographically) and supporting institutional strengthening. Through the prism of integrated market transformation, Phase II will remain fully aligned with leading strategies and policy frameworks developed by the Government of Egypt, supporting counterparts in reaching their respective objectives while further po</narrative>
  </description>
